
# <type>(<scope>)!: <description>
#
# [optional body]
#
# [optional footer(s)]
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits 1.0.0: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
#
# Header
#   type         Required. One of:
#                  feat      a new feature
#                  fix       a bug fix
#                  build     build system or external dependencies
#                  chore     maintenance that does not change behavior
#                  ci        CI configuration and scripts
#                  docs      documentation only
#                  perf      performance improvement
#                  refactor  restructuring without behavior change
#                  revert    revert of a previous commit
#                  style     formatting only, no change in meaning
#                  test      adding or correcting tests
#   (scope)      Optional. A noun for the affected area, e.g. (checker).
#   !            Optional. Marks a breaking change.
#   description  Required. Imperative mood, no trailing period.
#                72 characters or fewer for the whole header is recommended.
#
# Body
#   One blank line after the header. Explain what changed and why.
#   Wrap lines at 72 characters.
#
# Footers
#   One blank line after the body. Format: `Token: value`, using hyphens
#   in multi-word tokens (e.g. `Refs: #123`, `Reviewed-by: Name`).
#   Breaking changes: `BREAKING CHANGE: <description>`.
#
# Lines starting with '#' are removed. Leaving the message unedited
# aborts the commit.
